    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47889" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ternārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		terni, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>containing</i> or <i>consisting of three</i>,
				<i>ternary.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrobes,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of three feet</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 2, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numerus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 11 praef.</span></i>
			 — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ternārĭus</span></b> , ii,
				m., for triens, <i>a third of an</i>
			as, Pelag. Vet. 16.</div>
